Families looking for **children's activities in Rock Hill, SC** often visit places like the Rock Hill Children's Museum or enjoy a relaxing afternoon at Fountain Park. These are wonderful places for children to learn, explore, and grow. At **Resurrection Anglican Church**, we believe children also need a place where they can grow spiritually—learning the story of God's love and discovering their place in His Church.

### Forming the Next Generation

We are grateful for the many young families in our congregation. Children and young adults make up nearly one-third of our church, and we take seriously the Lord's call to help raise them in the truth of the gospel.

During our Sunday service, we provide **nursery care and age-appropriate teaching for preschool through fifth grade** during the Scripture readings and sermon. For the remainder of the service—especially during Holy Communion—children worship alongside the congregation. We believe this rhythm helps children grow in faith while allowing parents space to worship and be spiritually refreshed.

### God's Big Story

Our teaching is built around **God's Big Story**, an Anglican curriculum that helps children understand the Bible as one unified story of God's faithful love through Jesus Christ. Rather than learning isolated Bible stories, children begin to see how the whole Bible points to Jesus and how they are invited to be part of God's great story.

Our Children's Director thoughtfully adapts these lessons to serve the needs of our parish and help children engage deeply with Scripture.

### A Place for Families in Rock Hill

Rock Hill is a wonderful place to raise children, and families often spend time enjoying local landmarks like the Rock Hill Children's Museum or gathering in the heart of the city around Fountain Park.

At **Resurrection Anglican Church**, our desire is to provide something just as meaningful—a community where children are known, loved, and formed in the faith. If you are searching for a **children's ministry in Rock Hill, SC** or a **family-friendly church**, we would love to welcome you.

Our hope is that every child who comes through our doors will come to know Jesus Christ and grow as part of His Church.
